  "worked_solution": "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ by substituting the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =A{e}^{-3(0)}+B{e}^{-2(0)}+4(0){e}^{-2(0)} \\\\ 1 & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Differentiating $y$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=-3A{e}^{-3x}-2B{e}^{-2x}-8x{e}^{-2x}+4{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=1$ into the derivative gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-3A{e}^{-3(0)}-2B{e}^{-2(0)}-8(0){e}^{-2(0)}+4{e}^{-2(0)} \\\\ 1 & =-3A-2B+4 \\\\ -3 & =-3A-2B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A+B=1 \\\\ -3A-2B=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=1,B=0.$\n\nFinally, since $A=1$ and $B=0,$ we have the following solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-3x}+4x{e}^{-2x}\n$$",
